<!-- ======================================================
     DECISION FRAMEWORK
====================================================== -->

<section class="section soft-green">

<div class="section-inner">

<div class="section-heading">

<div class="section-number">
04 / DECISION FRAMEWORK
</div>

<h2>
Choose opportunities by constraints, not excitement.
</h2>

<p>
An opportunity isn't good simply because it sounds impressive.
Evaluate whether it actually fits your situation.
</p>

</div>


<table class="decision-table">

<tr>
<th>What matters?</th>
<th>Look for</th>
<th>Be careful about</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Speed</td>
<td>Short training, paid work, apprenticeships, immediate applications</td>
<td>Long programs with no clear employment outcome</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Low Cost</td>
<td>Free education, grants, scholarships, employer-paid training</td>
<td>Expensive programs with vague promises</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Experience</td>
<td>Projects, internships, apprenticeships, volunteer work</td>
<td>Collecting credentials without practical evidence</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Income Growth</td>
<td>Skills with advancement, demand, specialization, and portability</td>
<td>Only comparing today's starting salary</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Remote Work</td>
<td>Digitally deliverable skills and remote-capable occupations</td>
<td>Assuming every online job is legitimate</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Credential</td>
<td>Qualifications explicitly valued by target employers</td>
<td>Collecting unrelated certificates</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Mobility</td>
<td>Relocation programs, international pathways, remote employment</td>
<td>Moving without researching actual employment conditions</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Independence</td>
<td>Freelancing, entrepreneurship, products, services</td>
<td>Starting without validating whether people will pay</td>
</tr>

</table>

</div>

</section>


